[[00:01:47.490]]
SPEAKER 4 (HIGHER-PITCHED VOICE)
administration now has retreated from its constitutional arguments in public and claims that at least the War Powers Resolution does not forbid the strikes. because we're not involved in "hostilities" against Libya. Imagine that the shoe were on the other foot, that Libya was bombing us. Would we view the Libyan Air Force's bombings of our infrastructure as a hostile act? Of course we would. Last week, a member of the other chamber called the President's arguments "cute." I would use a different term: "embarrassing."

[[00:02:21.760]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
It's

[[00:02:22.250]]
